    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (32 tests, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` create pipeline now emits an audit line after a successful save.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`:\n- Logs via `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")` at INFO, carrying the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`.\n- Reads the persisted owner via `@Val Owner`, following the project's Out/@Val state-passing convention.\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`:\n- Inserted an `audit` step between `save` and `respond` (with `govern: [ transaction ]` like its neighbors), so the owner already has its persisted id and its assigned `customerCode` when the line is emitted.\n\nThe step order matters: it runs after `SaveOwner` (id assigned) and after `AssignCustomerCode` / `BuildOwner` (customerCode and business-day-adjusted registrationDate set). The observed audit line confirms the format matches what the test reads back from the GET response \u2014 e.g. `AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-08-17` (`LocalDate.toString()` yields the same ISO date the JSON response serializes).",
